From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:37:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A folded plain-text user message renders only its first ten
 source lines, at most 4,096 characters, until the reader shows it all, which
 still overflows the eight-line preview whenever the whole prompt would, so
 the clip, the toggle and Copy message are unchanged while a 131 KB prompt
 (the benchmark's long rows) is no longer laid out behind the clip; the plain
 prompt renderer moves beside the fold as HighlightedPromptText,
 message-part.tsx's ceiling falls to its measured 2,150 lines, and the app's
 line budget is the measured 107,810.

