@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ A logic change here is its own slice, proven by the transcript corpus (flow 30,
 - A user message's header (`user-message-head.ts`) names the engine agent the message carries, capitalized, else the harness the session runs (`harnessLabel` on the data context, the contract's `harnessProductLabel`), then the model. Only OpenCode has agents, so only a prompt the person aimed at one names an agent; the app never writes the engine's default into a prompt or its echo, and a header reading "Build" on a Claude or Pi session is the defect this rule removes.
 - The data context (`data.tsx`): `DataProvider` and `useData()` carry the placement folder, the session's harness label, and the host's callbacks (session and task hrefs, first-party tool hrefs, subagent resolution, file URLs, tool images, and `loadToolBody` for a tool part a page sent as its header). A header-only tool row (`part.headerOnly`) draws its collapsed header from the input and metadata the header reads, can open although it holds no body (`bodyPending` on `BasicTool`), and asks for its whole part when it opens; a patch's header keeps each file's path and counts (`patchFiles(files, headerOnly)`). `useOptionalData()` is for renderers that also mount outside a session.
 - Parts (`message-part.tsx`): the registry from `part.type` and tool name to a renderer, one registry entry per harness alias, and the user-message, text, reasoning, tool, image and file renderers.
-- User-message text shares `FoldedUserMessageBody` for plain text and markdown. Rendered content beyond eight lines starts clipped without a fade, with a visible Show all / Show less button inside the card's shared surface. A ResizeObserver reads actual content height, including width and typography changes; its subscription ends with the component. Expansion stays local to that mounted message. Collapse brings the preview back into view, and focusing a clipped link expands it. Attachments stay outside the preview, and copy always reads the complete original text. Assistant replies and work/turn folds keep their own behavior. Flow 30 (`30-user-message-fold.spec.ts`, desktop and phone) and the `long-user-message` corpus case cover this presentation.
+- User-message text shares `FoldedUserMessageBody` for plain text and markdown. Rendered content beyond eight lines starts clipped without a fade, with a visible Show all / Show less button inside the card's shared surface. Plain text is drawn by `HighlightedPromptText`, which marks its file and agent mentions, in the same module. While folded, plain text renders only its first ten source lines, at most 4,096 characters (`foldedPreviewLength`): that prefix overflows the eight-line preview whenever the whole text would, so the clip and the toggle are unchanged, and a 131 KB prompt is not laid out behind the clip. Markdown renders whole. A ResizeObserver reads actual content height, including width and typography changes; its subscription ends with the component. Expansion stays local to that mounted message. Collapse brings the preview back into view, and focusing a clipped link expands it. Attachments stay outside the preview, and copy always reads the complete original text. Assistant replies and work/turn folds keep their own behavior. Flow 30 (`30-user-message-fold.spec.ts`, desktop and phone) and the `long-user-message` corpus case cover this presentation.
